cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the associated paper (preferred-citation)."
title: "mmc-sysid-benchmark: System identification benchmark for a grid-connected MMC (RTDS/RSCAD)"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<owner>/mmc-sysid-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a controlled simulation-based benchmark of classical,
  nonlinear/ML-based, and hybrid/physics-informed system identification
  methods, applied to a high-fidelity grid-connected modular multilevel
  converter (MMC) model of the CIGRE B4.57 MMC-HVDC system simulated in
  RTDS/RSCAD.
keywords:
  - system identification
  - converter-dominated power systems
  - modular multilevel converter
  - HVDC
  - subspace identification
  - impedance identification
  - machine learning
  - physics-informed learning
  - RTDS
